exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib dev perf slow matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib dev perf slow [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Recent slow queries from the collector's Redis ring buffer (procedure, durationMs, entity, params, timestamp). Developer-only.
  Permissions: requires isSystemAdmin or isDeveloper.

FLAGS
  --limit NUMBER    Max rows (default: 50)
  --env STRING    Environment buffer to read (default: backend's current env; discover via \`ib dev perf config\`)

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  ListEnvelope<{ procedure, durationMs, entity, params, timestamp }> & { totalCount?, environment? } (+truncated:true when the page filled the limit)

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not a developer        → requires isSystemAdmin or isDeveloper
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - SQL durations cover the executeQuery (cache-runner) path only — raw getConnection() queries are not timed.
  - Threshold to be 'slow' is the collector's SLOW_QUERY_THRESHOLD_MS (default 1000ms) — see \`ib dev perf config\`.

SEE ALSO
  ib dev perf stats, ib dev perf config

EXAMPLES
  ib dev perf slow
  ib dev perf slow --limit 20 --env production
"
`;

