  ib dev schema trigger keikka_after_ins_trig,tyomaaPerson_after_ins_trig
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib dev schema triggers matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib dev schema triggers [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  List dbo triggers with their parent table, timing (AFTER / INSTEAD OF), the events that fire them, and whether they are disabled. Narrow to one table with --table. Developer-only.
  Permissions: requires developer access (isSystemAdmin or isDeveloper).

FLAGS
  --search STRING    Filter object names by substring
  --limit NUMBER    Max rows (max 1000). The default CAPS the catalogue — dbo holds ~240 tables and ~535 procs, so a default \`procs\`/\`tables\` read is a PARTIAL list; pass --limit 1000 whenever you intend to enumerate. (default: 200)
  --table STRING    Only triggers whose parent table is this (exact name)

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { items: [{ name, table, timing:'AFTER'|'INSTEAD OF', events:['INSERT'|'UPDATE'|'DELETE'], disabled, type:'trigger' }], nextCursor: null, count, truncated?, hint? }. \`truncated: true\` (with a \`hint\` naming the way out) means the row cap bit and this page is NOT the whole catalogue — it also prints a warning on stderr. Never conclude an object does not exist from a truncated page; re-run with --limit 1000 or --search first.

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (client-side)  --limit is not an integer >= 1, rejected locally before any request → pass a positive integer; max is 1000, and the 200 default returns a PARTIAL catalogue — pass \`--limit 1000\` whenever you intend to enumerate
  exit 4 (HTTP 400)  Invalid name (letters/digits/underscore only) → use the bare object name, no schema prefix
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not a developer        → run \`ib auth whoami\`; if not a developer, \`ib auth login\` as a developer account (same person re-login won't grant it). Gate is server-side — a new DB flag only applies once --endpoint's backend is redeployed.
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - Trigger bodies carry real business logic here (keikka_after_ins_trig creates keikkaBetoni/toimitus/keikkaPerson rows), so a table's writers are not fully described by its procs alone.
  - \`ib dev schema table <name>\` already lists that table's triggers in its \`triggers\` summary — use this command to search across tables or to filter by name.

EXAMPLES
  ib dev schema triggers
  ib dev schema triggers --table keikka
  ib dev schema triggers --search updateLastActive
"
`;

