exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib jerry admin request resend matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib jerry admin request resend <requestId> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Re-match providers and notify the NEW ones (POST /api/admin/jerry-requests/:id/resend). Safe to repeat: providers already on the recipient list keep their notifiedAt/viewedAt/declinedAt and are NOT re-emailed, so a resend with an unchanged match set is a no-op (notifiedCount 0). System-admin only. Requires --reason.
  Permissions: requires isSystemAdmin.

ARGUMENTS
  <requestId> NUMBER    pumppuRequestId (required)

FLAGS
  --reason STRING    Audit-log reason (X-Action-Reason); REQUIRED

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            Validate without persisting (server-side X-Dry-Run). Returns the would-be response.
                       If the backend does NOT honour it, the CLI exits 6 rather than reporting a write as a preview.
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification, stored in audit log. REQUIRED.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { success: true, status: 'open' | 'no_supply', providerCount, notifiedCount } or { dryRun: true, wouldUpdate: { pumppuRequestId, status } }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not a system admin     → use a system-admin token
  exit 4 (HTTP 409)  Wrong state            → request not in a resendable state
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - providerCount = companies matching the worksite now; notifiedCount = of those, how many were newly added and emailed.
  - Use it to reach a provider that only just became eligible — it will not spam the ones that already ignored the request.

EXAMPLES
  ib jerry admin request resend 41 --reason "uusi tarjoaja alueelle"
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib jerry admin request stats matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib jerry admin request stats [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Windowed tarjouspyyntö rollup — per-bucket counts with the status split and offer summary (GET /api/admin/jerry-requests/stats). The aggregate sibling of \`request list\`: answers 'how many per week?' in one call instead of pulling every row and bucketing client-side. System-admin only.
  Permissions: requires isSystemAdmin.

FLAGS
  --from STRING    createdAt from (YYYY-MM-DD/today/yesterday)
  --to STRING    createdAt to (inclusive)
  --group-by STRING    Bucket by week | month | status (default: week)

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { groupBy, from, to, buckets: [{ bucket, total, byStatus: { [status]: count }, offerCount, withOffers }], totals: { total, byStatus, offerCount, withOffers } }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (HTTP 400)  Invalid groupBy        → use week, month or status
  exit 4 (client-side)  --group-by is not week/month/status → pass one of week, month, status
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not a system admin     → use a system-admin token
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - Bucketing happens in SQL in HELSINKI time, not UTC: a Sunday-evening request belongs to the week a Finnish reader would put it in. Weeks are ISO weeks labelled with the ISO YEAR, so a week straddling New Year stays one bucket — 2027-01-03 is \`2026-W53\`, not \`2027-W53\`.
  - \`withOffers\` counts requests that received at least one non-draft offer; \`offerCount\` sums the offers themselves. With --group-by status the bucket IS the status, so byStatus has a single key — useful as a plain status breakdown for the window.
  - Unlike \`request list\` there is no row cap, so totals stay correct as volume grows (the list caps at 300 and would silently under-count a client-side rollup).

SEE ALSO
  ib jerry admin request list, ib jerry admin searches funnel

EXAMPLES
  ib jerry admin request stats --from 2026-05-01
  ib jerry admin request stats --from 2026-01-01 --group-by month
  ib jerry admin request stats --from 2026-05-01 --group-by status
"
`;

