exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib jerry provider-settings get matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib jerry provider-settings get [flags]
  (also: ib jerry provider-settings show)

DESCRIPTION
  Read a provider company's BetoniJerry settings — contact person, opening hours, company description, maintainsOrderInfo (GET /api/jerry-provider-settings). Defaults to the caller's own company; --asiakas targets another company you have edit rights on. Returns defaults when no row exists yet.
  Permissions: requires edit-tier on the target company (tarjousAdmin / company admin).

FLAGS
  --asiakas NUMBER    Target company asiakasId (default: your own)

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { asiakasId, jerryPersonId, jerryPersonName, jerryPersonPhone, jerryPersonEmail, openingHours, companyDescription, maintainsOrderInfo, website, publicSlug, publicListingConsentAt, publicListingConsentBy }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  No edit rights on company → use a tarjousAdmin/admin token for that company
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

EXAMPLES
  ib jerry provider-settings get
  ib jerry provider-settings get --asiakas 1402
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib jerry provider-settings set matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib jerry provider-settings set [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Upsert a provider company's BetoniJerry settings (PUT /api/jerry-provider-settings). Partial-payload-safe: only the body keys present are written (omit a key to preserve it). jerryPersonId must belong to the target company. --asiakas targets another company. Returns the FULL saved settings (no follow-up GET needed) plus changed:boolean (whether anything actually changed vs an idempotent no-op). companyDescription is nvarchar — ä/ö are preserved. Requires --reason. Writable keys: jerryPersonId, openingHours, companyDescription, maintainsOrderInfo, website, publicSlug, publicListingConsent. \`publicListingConsent\` is a BOOLEAN intent flag — the server stamps publicListingConsentAt/By from your token; never send a timestamp. Re-granting an already-granted consent does not re-stamp the original date. On Windows PowerShell use --from-json <file>: PowerShell splits a quoted --body value on its inner double-quotes.
  Permissions: requires edit-tier on the target company (tarjousAdmin / company admin).

FLAGS
  --body JSON    JSON: { jerryPersonId?, offerNotificationEmail?, openingHours?, companyDescription?, maintainsOrderInfo?, website?, publicSlug?, publicListingConsent? }. Mutually exclusive with --from-json. ⚠ Windows PowerShell splits this argument on its inner double-quotes, so inline JSON arrives mangled and exits 4 as a too-many-arguments usage error — use --from-json <file|-> there, or typed flags (fb#437; see \`ib help shell-quoting\`).
  --from-json STRING    Read the JSON body from a file (or - for stdin); shell-safe alternative to --body. Mutually exclusive with --body.
  --email STRING    Address tarjouspyyntö mail is DELIVERED to (offerNotificationEmail). May be a shared inbox — it is a mailbox, not a login, so jerryPersonId stays a named person who signs in. Wins over jerryPersonId's own address when set, and over the same key in --body; pass "" to clear — PowerShell DROPS a bare "", so use \`--email=\` there (same meaning in bash; \`ib help shell-quoting\`) and fall back to it.
  --asiakas NUMBER    Target company asiakasId (default: your own)
  --reason STRING    Audit-log reason (X-Action-Reason); REQUIRED

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            Validate without persisting (server-side X-Dry-Run). Returns the would-be response.
                       If the backend does NOT honour it, the CLI exits 6 rather than reporting a write as a preview.
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification, stored in audit log. REQUIRED.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { asiakasId, jerryPersonId, jerryPersonName, jerryPersonPhone, jerryPersonEmail, offerNotificationEmail, openingHours, companyDescription, maintainsOrderInfo, website, publicSlug, publicListingConsentAt, publicListingConsentBy, changed } · { dryRun: true, wouldUpdate: {...} } on --dry-run

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (HTTP 400)  Invalid field / contact not in company → check jerryPersonId belongs to the company; offerNotificationEmail must be a valid address
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  No edit rights on company → use a tarjousAdmin/admin token for that company
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - On Windows PowerShell inline --body JSON often fails (the shell strips the inner double-quotes) — pass --from-json <file|-> (a file, or - for stdin) to avoid shell quoting entirely.
  - Before fb#532 jerryPersonId did both jobs — WHERE offer mail lands and WHO signs in — which pushed operators into configuring shared login accounts. The welcome email forbids those on GDPR/audit grounds, and the one account set up that way went three weeks without a single login.

EXAMPLES
  ib jerry provider-settings set --body '{"openingHours":"ma-pe 7-16","maintainsOrderInfo":true}' --reason "update opening hours"
  ib jerry provider-settings set --from-json ./settings.json --reason "update opening hours"
  ib jerry provider-settings set --body '{"jerryPersonId":6233}' --asiakas 1402 --reason "set contact"
  ib jerry provider-settings set --email tarjoukset@yritys.fi --asiakas 1409 --reason "route offers to the shared inbox"
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib jerry request cancel matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib jerry request cancel <requestId> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Cancel your OWN pump request (customer-side) — allowed only while no live offer exists (POST /api/pumppuRequests/:id/cancel). Sets status='cancelled'. Requires --reason.

ARGUMENTS
  <requestId> NUMBER    pumppuRequestId you own (required)

FLAGS
  --reason STRING    Audit-log reason (X-Action-Reason); REQUIRED

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            Validate without persisting (server-side X-Dry-Run). Returns the would-be response.
                       If the backend does NOT honour it, the CLI exits 6 rather than reporting a write as a preview.
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification, stored in audit log. REQUIRED.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { success: true, status: 'cancelled' } or { dryRun: true, wouldUpdate: { pumppuRequestId, status } }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 5 (HTTP 404)  Request not found / not yours → verify the requestId and that you own it
  exit 4 (HTTP 409)  Already has offers     → cannot cancel once an offer arrived
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

EXAMPLES
  ib jerry request cancel 88 --reason "tilaus peruuntui"
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib jerry request create matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib jerry request create [<address>] [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Create a customer pump request / tarjouspyyntö (POST /api/pumppuRequests). Any authenticated user — this is the CUSTOMER side (distinct from \`ib jerry offer create\`, the provider bid). The worksite address is given positionally OR via --address (exactly one; both allowed only if they agree). The server geocodes the address and inserts the request as status:'open', immediately visible to every geographically-matching provider. Omit --asiakas to bill it to your auto-created private BetoniJerry customer account; pass --asiakas to use a company you have access to. Requires --reason.
  Auth: requires login (any authenticated user).

ARGUMENTS
  <address> STRING    Worksite address (osoite); pass it here OR as --address (exactly one) (optional)

FLAGS
  --address STRING    Worksite address (osoite); alias for the positional
  --pump-at STRING    Pump datetime (pumppausaika; ISO, REQUIRED), e.g. 2026-06-17T09:00:00+03:00
  --m3 NUMBER    Concrete volume m³ (maaraM3; REQUIRED, > 0)
  --boom NUMBER    Required boom reach m (puomi) (default: 0)
  --duration NUMBER    Pump duration hours (kesto)
  --line-length NUMBER    Hose line length m (linjanPituus)
  --notes STRING    Free-text description shown to providers (kuvaus)
  --asiakas NUMBER    Customer asiakasId (omit → your private BetoniJerry account)
  --reason STRING    Audit-log reason (X-Action-Reason); REQUIRED

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            Validate without persisting (server-side X-Dry-Run). Returns the would-be response.
                       If the backend does NOT honour it, the CLI exits 6 rather than reporting a write as a preview.
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification, stored in audit log. REQUIRED.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { pumppuRequestId, status:'open', asiakasId, personId, tyomaaId, geocoded } · { dryRun:true, wouldCreate:{ asiakasId, osoite, pumppuAika, totalM3, requiredPuomi, pumppuKesto, requiredLinja, notes }, validation:{ ok:true } } on --dry-run

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (client-side)  Address missing, or given BOTH positionally and via --address with different values → pass the address exactly once — positional or --address
  exit 4 (client-side)  --m3 is not a number > 0 → pass --m3 as a positive number of cubic metres
  exit 4 (HTTP 400)  Server-side validation: pumppausaika not a parseable datetime, whitespace-only osoite, or non-numeric asiakasId/puomi → pass --pump-at as a full ISO datetime (e.g. 2026-06-17T09:00:00+03:00) and a non-empty address
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  No access to --asiakas → omit --asiakas, or target a company you belong to
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - Customer side: creates the tarjouspyyntö itself, NOT a provider offer (that is \`ib jerry offer create\`).
  - Created as status:'open' → immediately fans out to matching provider inboxes. Run \`ib jerry check-address\` first to preview which providers (if any) cover the address.
  - --dry-run runs the server's synchronous validation and echoes the would-be request, touching no DB (no asiakas resolve/auto-create, no geocode, no insert) — so a bad --pump-at/--m3 still 400s under --dry-run.

SEE ALSO
  ib jerry check-address, ib jerry request list, ib jerry offer create

EXAMPLES
  ib jerry request create "Mannerheimintie 1, Helsinki" --pump-at 2026-06-17T09:00:00+03:00 --m3 30 --reason "tilaus"
  ib jerry request create --address "Mannerheimintie 1, Helsinki" --pump-at 2026-06-17T09:00:00+03:00 --m3 30 --boom 24 --notes "ahdas piha" --reason "tilaus"
  ib jerry request create "Mannerheimintie 1, Helsinki" --pump-at 2026-06-17T09:00:00+03:00 --m3 30 --dry-run --reason "preview"
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib jerry request decline matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib jerry request decline <requestId> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Decline a request as a provider WITHOUT making an offer (POST /api/pumppuRequests/:id/decline). Your company bows out; --reason is stored and shown to the customer (who is emailed + pushed that a provider passed). The request leaves your Avoimet tab (moves to Päättyneet). Blocked (409) if you already have an active offer — use \`ib jerry offer withdraw\` instead. Idempotent. Requires provider role + --reason.
  Permissions: requires provider company (isPumppuToimittaja).

ARGUMENTS
  <requestId> NUMBER    pumppuRequestId you were sent (required)

FLAGS
  --reason STRING    Decline reason — stored, shown to the customer, and audited (X-Action-Reason); REQUIRED

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            Validate without persisting (server-side X-Dry-Run). Returns the would-be response.
                       If the backend does NOT honour it, the CLI exits 6 rather than reporting a write as a preview.
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification, stored in audit log. REQUIRED.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { success: true, declined: true, hasOtherProviders } (or { …, alreadyDeclined: true }) · { dryRun: true, wouldDecline: { pumppuRequestId, reason } } on --dry-run

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 5 (HTTP 404)  Request not found / not a recipient → verify the requestId and that it was sent to your company
  exit 4 (HTTP 409)  You already have an offer → withdraw the offer instead (ib jerry offer withdraw)
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not a provider         → switch to a provider company (company switch)
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

EXAMPLES
  ib jerry request decline 88 --reason "kalusto varattu kyseiselle päivälle"
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib jerry request get matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib jerry request get <requestId> [flags]
  (also: ib jerry request show)

DESCRIPTION
  Get one pump request. Default is the customer-owned recap (GET /api/pumppuRequests/:id, scoped to the caller's personId). --provider returns the provider-facing detail (GET /api/pumppuRequests/:id/provider-detail, requires provider role) including your own offer + attachments. This returns the FULL customer lead (name, address, lat/lng, phone, email) to every matched provider as soon as the request is open — it is NOT masked pre-acceptance. Masking applies to the \`--open\` inbox list and the fan-out email, not here.
  Permissions: requires --provider: provider company (isPumppuToimittaja).

ARGUMENTS
  <requestId> NUMBER    pumppuRequestId (required)

FLAGS
  --provider    Provider-facing detail view (provider role)

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  default: { pumppuRequestId, status, asiakasId, maaraM3, osoite, lat, lng, ... } | --provider: { request:{...}, ownOffer:{...}|null, ownAttachments:[…], requestAttachments:[…], messageThreadId }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 5 (HTTP 404)  Request not found / not yours → verify requestId (and that you own it, or use --provider)
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not a provider (for --provider) → switch to a provider company
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

EXAMPLES
  ib jerry request get 4012
  ib jerry request get 4012 --provider
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib jerry request list matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib jerry request list [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  List BetoniJerry pump requests (tarjouspyynnöt). Default --mine returns the caller's own requests (GET /api/pumppuRequests/mine). --open returns the provider inbox of open requests in your delivery area (GET /api/pumppuRequests/open) and requires a provider company (isPumppuToimittaja); customer PII is masked there until your offer is accepted. --provider is the provider's own lifecycle view (GET /api/pumppuRequests/provider-list) — also provider-only, and includes your sent offers — selected by --tab <avoimet|tarjotut|voitetut|paattyneet> (default avoimet): avoimet = open requests to bid on, tarjotut = ones you have offered on (offer pending), voitetut = won (your offer accepted/confirmed), paattyneet = ended (expired, no_supply, or lost to another provider). --status (CSV) and --limit apply to --mine only. Whole-market visibility is system-admin only.
  Permissions: requires --open / --provider: provider company (isPumppuToimittaja).

FLAGS
  --open    Provider inbox of open requests in your delivery area (provider role)
  --mine    Your own requests (default)
  --status STRING    Filter --mine by status (CSV: open,pending_verification,accepted,cancelled,expired,no_supply)
  --limit NUMBER    Max rows for --mine (server caps at 200) (default: 100)
  --provider    Provider lifecycle view via /provider-list (incl. sent offers)
  --tab STRING    With --provider: which lifecycle tab to return (avoimet|tarjotut|voitetut|paattyneet) (default: avoimet)

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  ListEnvelope<{ pumppuRequestId, status, createdAt, sentAt?, osoite, formattedAddress, totalM3|maaraM3, ... }> (fields differ between --mine and --open; --open is PII-masked)

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (client-side)  --limit is not an integer >= 1, rejected locally before any request → pass a positive integer; the server caps \`--mine\` at 200, so narrow with \`--status\` rather than raising the cap
  exit 4 (HTTP 400)  Unknown --tab          → use one of avoimet, tarjotut, voitetut, paattyneet (server-validated)
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not a provider (for --open / --provider) → switch to a provider company, or use --mine
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

SEE ALSO
  ib jerry admin request list

EXAMPLES
  ib jerry request list
  ib jerry request list --open
  ib jerry request list --mine --status open,accepted --limit 50
  ib jerry request list --provider --tab tarjotut
"
`;

