exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib person absences matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib person absences --from <from> --to <to> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Staff absences (personPvm 'pois' rows — vacation / sick / etc.) in a date range. Staff-wide and person-keyed: the canonical 'who is away' query. An absent person cannot be set as a day driver, so this is also the driver-availability blocker list.
  Permissions: requires auth.page.grid.read.
  Timezone: dates interpreted in active company timezone (Europe/Helsinki).

FLAGS
  --from DATE    Start date YYYY-MM-DD (or today/yesterday/tomorrow) (required)
  --to DATE    End date YYYY-MM-DD (or today/yesterday/tomorrow) (required)
  --person NUMBER    Filter to one personId

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  ListEnvelope<{ personId, name, date, status, statusName }>

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Permission denied      → check auth.page.grid.read
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - Read-only — setting absence status is not exposed by the CLI in v1.
  - Reuses /api/cli/driver/absences server-side; \`ib vehicle driver available\` already excludes these from the assignable pool. Deploy-gated.

SEE ALSO
  ib vehicle driver available, ib person day set

EXAMPLES
  ib person absences --from today --to today
  ib person absences --from 2026-06-01 --to 2026-06-30 --person 123
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib person activity matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib person activity <personId> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Login / security-event / impersonation history for one person: lastLoginTime, personLog type-1 logins, SecurityEventLog rows for the person's email — all event types (SUCCESSFUL_LOGIN plus lockout/brute-force/rate-limit), each with eventType/method/ip (source once persisted) — and impersonation rows as-target and as-actor. Developer-only — the data includes IPs/emails.
  Permissions: requires developer access (isSystemAdmin or isDeveloper).

ARGUMENTS
  <personId> NUMBER    person.personId (required)

FLAGS
  --limit NUMBER    Max rows per list (capped at 1000) (default: 100)

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { personId, email, lastLoginTime, logins:[{entryTime}], securityEvents:[{eventType,method,source,ip,timestamp}], impersonations:{ asTarget:[{actorPersonId,entryTime,type,sessionId,endReason?}], asActor:[{targetPersonId,entryTime,type,sessionId,endReason?}] } }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (HTTP 400)  personId is not a positive integer → pass a numeric personId
  exit 5 (HTTP 404)  no person with that id → check the id with \`ib person get <id>\`
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Permission denied      → check developer access (isSystemAdmin or isDeveloper)
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - Developer-gated server-side and hidden from non-developer discovery.
  - personLog type-1 counts credential logins AND token-refresh/impersonation bootstraps; cross-check securityEvents (credential-only) to tell them apart. Deploy-gated (no-op until the puminet5api backend deploys).

SEE ALSO
  ib person log, ib person get

EXAMPLES
  ib person activity 63
  ib person activity 63 --limit 20
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib person companies matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib person companies [<personId>] [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  List the companies (asiakkaat) a person belongs to, in the notion backend AUTHORIZATION uses: every company with an asiakasPerson attachment (or where the person is the asiakas contact person), which is the same set that mints the JWT \`asiakasesWithTypes\` claim. Each row carries the roles + toimittaja flags held there and \`activeMembership\` (does the person also hold an enabled, in-validity role?). personId defaults to the caller. Reverse of \`customer person list\`.
  Permissions: requires self, company admin (asiakasAdmin/hrAdmin/asiakasOwner) in a company shared with the target, or developer.

ARGUMENTS
  <personId> NUMBER    personId (defaults to caller) (optional)

FLAGS
  --as-token    Report the ACTIVE token's own \`asiakasesWithTypes\` claim verbatim instead of querying — literally what the backend authorizes on. Offline; self-only (a token carries only its bearer's memberships).

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  ListEnvelope<{ asiakasId, name, roles: string[]|null, isTyomaaAsiakas, isPumppuToimittaja, isBetoniToimittaja, isLattiaToimittaja (each boolean|null), activeMembership }> + { personId, source: 'asiakas_listForPerson'|'person_getUserAsiakasList', hint? }. With --as-token: ListEnvelope<{ asiakasId, roles, is*Toimittaja, isTyomaaAsiakas }> + { personId, source:'jwt-claim', mintedAt: string|null, hint } — no company names (the JWT carries none for non-active companies).

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not authorized to read that person's companies → you need company admin in a company you share with them, or developer access; drop the personId to read your own
  exit 4 (client-side)  --as-token given with another person's personId → --as-token only reports YOUR token's claim — drop the personId, or drop --as-token to query the backend
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - \`activeMembership: false\` means AUTHORIZED but holding no live role there — still a company the backend lets the person act in. Do not read it as 'not a member'.
  - Two membership notions exist in the DB and they disagree by design: \`asiakas_listForPerson\` (this command, and the JWT claim) counts any attachment; \`person_getUserAsiakasList\` additionally requires an undeleted attachment with an enabled, in-validity role and is always a SUBSET. Before fb#395 this command reported the subset while every authorization path read the superset.
  - \`--as-token\` is the ground truth for 'why did that endpoint 403 me': provider routes (e.g. tarjous/pumppu endpoints) resolve their toimittaja flags straight from this claim. It is a SNAPSHOT taken at \`mintedAt\` — a company added or role granted since is absent until the token is re-minted (\`ib company switch\`, re-login, refresh). \`mintedAt\` is null on compact/short-shape tokens (signed without \`iat\`); treat null as unknown, not as just-now.
  - \`source: 'person_getUserAsiakasList'\` means the backend route is not deployed yet, so the rows are the narrower ACTIVE-membership subset and \`roles\`/\`is*\` come back **null** — meaning 'this source cannot report them', NOT 'no roles'. Every row that source returns provably holds at least one role. The \`hint\` field says so too.

SEE ALSO
  ib company list, ib person me, ib person role list, ib customer person list

EXAMPLES
  ib person companies
  ib person companies 5351
  ib person companies --as-token
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib person create matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib person create [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Create a person. REQUIRED: --first, --last. --email is OPTIONAL (personEmail is nullable; phone-only contacts are fine and the email can be added later via \`ib person update\`). --asiakas defaults to your active company. Returns the created person record (clean {personId, ...}), NOT the raw SQL recordset. With --get-or-create a duplicate email returns the existing person (reused:true) when that person is visible to you (the email dedup is global, so an email owned by a company you can't access errors with guidance instead) — useful for idempotent bulk onboarding. NOTE: creating under a non-active owned company (--asiakas <other>) sets ownership but no membership, and the record is synthesized in the reply because the read-back is scoped to your active company. Use typed flags or --body JSON (typed flags win). Requires --reason. Use --global to create a GLOBAL, self-managing person (ownerAsiakasId=null) discoverable across companies; --global and --asiakas are mutually exclusive.
  Permissions: requires auth.page.person.edit.

FLAGS
  --first STRING    personFirstName (REQUIRED)
  --last STRING    personLastName (REQUIRED)
  --phone STRING    personPhone
  --email STRING    personEmail (optional)
  --memo STRING    personMemo — free-text note/comment (optional)
  --asiakas NUMBER    Owner asiakasId (defaults to your active company)
  --global    Create a global, owner-less person (ownerAsiakasId=null). Mutually exclusive with --asiakas.
  --get-or-create    On a duplicate email, return the existing person (reused:true) when visible to you; an email owned by a company you can't access errors with guidance
  --body JSON    Raw JSON body, merged under typed flags (optional) ⚠ Windows PowerShell splits this argument on its inner double-quotes, so inline JSON arrives mangled and exits 4 as a too-many-arguments usage error — use --from-json <file|-> there, or typed flags (fb#437; see \`ib help shell-quoting\`).
  --from-json STRING    Read the JSON body from a file (or - for stdin); shell-safe alternative to --body. Mutually exclusive with --body.
  --reason STRING    Audit-log reason (X-Action-Reason); REQUIRED

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            Validate without persisting (server-side X-Dry-Run). Returns the would-be response.
                       If the backend does NOT honour it, the CLI exits 6 rather than reporting a write as a preview.
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification, stored in audit log. REQUIRED.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { personId, name, email, ... } (re-fetched) · with --get-or-create adds reused:boolean · dry-run: { dryRun: true, wouldCreate: ... }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (client-side)  --asiakas is not an integer >= 1, rejected locally before any request → pass a positive asiakasId (a company id) — \`ib company list\` shows the ones you can reach
  exit 4 (client-side)  A required field is missing (the message names which) → pass the flags the message names — --first and --last are required; email is optional
  exit 4 (client-side)  Both --global and --asiakas given — contradictory owner directives → pass one: --global for a self-managing person (ownerAsiakasId null), or --asiakas <id> to own it
  exit 4 (client-side)  --get-or-create matched an email owned by a company you cannot see, so it can neither reuse nor create → find the owner with \`ib person search --my-companies\`, or create with a different email
  exit 4 (HTTP 400)  Duplicate email without --get-or-create → add --get-or-create to reuse an existing visible person, or use a different email
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Permission denied      → check auth.page.person.edit
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - On Windows PowerShell inline --body JSON often fails (the shell strips the inner double-quotes) — prefer typed flags, or pass --from-json <file|-> (a file, or - for stdin) to avoid shell quoting entirely.

EXAMPLES
  ib person create --first Matti --last Virtanen --phone "+358501234567" --reason "phone contact"
  ib person create --first Matti --last Virtanen --email m@x.com --get-or-create --reason "onboard"
  ib person create --body '{"personFirstName":"Matti","personLastName":"M"}' --reason "onboard"
  ib person create --from-json ./person.json --reason "onboard"
  ib person create --first Matti --last Virtanen --global --reason "global self-managing person"
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib person day clear matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib person day clear --person <person> --date <date> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Delete a person's day row for a date (remove status entry). Requires --reason.
  Auth: requires login (any authenticated user).
  Timezone: dates interpreted in active company timezone (Europe/Helsinki).

FLAGS
  --person NUMBER    personId (required)
  --date DATE    Day YYYY-MM-DD (or today/yesterday/tomorrow) (required)

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            CLIENT-side preview: resolves locally, no write reaches the wire (works under --read-only).
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification, stored in audit log. REQUIRED.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  delete result | { dryRun:true, wouldDelete:{ personPvmId, date, status } | null } (with --dry-run)

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (HTTP 400)  Missing --reason       → supply --reason
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Requires Admin or HR Admin on the active company → use an Admin/HR account
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - Requires Admin or HR Admin (server-enforced).
  - --reason is hard-required (exits 4 without it).
  - Resolves the personPvmId via the day list; when no row exists it's a no-op (deleted:false).

SEE ALSO
  ib person day set, ib person day get

EXAMPLES
  ib person day clear --person 555 --date 2026-06-10 --reason 'loma peruttu'
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib person day get matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib person day get --person <person> --from <from> [flags]
  (also: ib person day show)

DESCRIPTION
  List a person's day rows (status / vehicle / text) over a date range
  Auth: requires login (any authenticated user).
  Timezone: dates interpreted in active company timezone (Europe/Helsinki).

FLAGS
  --person NUMBER    personId (required)
  --from DATE    Start date YYYY-MM-DD (or today/yesterday/tomorrow) (required)
  --to DATE    End date YYYY-MM-DD (default: --from)

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  ListEnvelope<{ personPvmId, date, statusId, status, pois, vehicleId, text }>

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - Scoped to the active company (same-tenant).
  - \`status\` is the personPvmStatus code; map statusId→friendly name via \`ib person day statuses\`.

SEE ALSO
  ib person day set, ib vehicle driver who

EXAMPLES
  ib person day get --person 555 --from today
  ib person day get --person 555 --from 2026-06-01 --to 2026-06-30
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib person day set matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib person day set --person <person> --date <date> --status <status> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Set a person's day availability status (vacation/sick/free/…). Requires --reason.
  Auth: requires login (any authenticated user).
  Timezone: dates interpreted in active company timezone (Europe/Helsinki).

FLAGS
  --person NUMBER    personId (required)
  --date DATE    Day YYYY-MM-DD (or today/yesterday/tomorrow) (required)
  --status STRING    personPvmStatusId or status name (see \`ib person day statuses\`) (required)
  --text STRING    Free-text note on the day row

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            CLIENT-side preview: resolves locally, no write reaches the wire (works under --read-only).
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification, stored in audit log. REQUIRED.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  personPvm save result | { dryRun:true, personId, date, wouldChange:{ status?, text? } } (with --dry-run)

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (HTTP 400)  Missing --reason or unknown/ambiguous --status → supply --reason; check \`ib person day statuses\`
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Requires Admin or HR Admin on the active company → use an Admin/HR account
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - Requires Admin or HR Admin (server-enforced) — Keikka Handler is NOT sufficient.
  - --status accepts an id or a name (resolved via \`ib person day statuses\`).
  - --reason is hard-required (exits 4 without it).
  - Read-merges the existing row so a re-set updates in place (no duplicate) and PRESERVES the existing vehicle assignment. It cannot CHANGE the vehicle — use \`ib vehicle driver assign\` for that (atomic).

SEE ALSO
  ib person day statuses, ib person day clear, ib vehicle driver assign

EXAMPLES
  ib person day set --person 555 --date tomorrow --status loma --reason 'kesäloma'
  ib person day set --person 555 --date 2026-06-10 --status 2 --dry-run --reason preview
"
`;

