exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib person email set-main matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib person email set-main <person> <email> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Promote one of a person's emails to be the PRIMARY (person.personEmail), demoting the previous primary into the alternatives (personEmails). The target must already be an address on this person (primary or alternative). Login is unaffected — every address resolves the person either way; this only changes which one is the displayed/primary address. Idempotent when already primary. Tenant-scoped like \`ib person email add\`. Requires --reason.
  Permissions: requires auth.page.person.edit.

ARGUMENTS
  <person> STRING    personId or a name resolved within your active company (required)
  <email> STRING    the person's email to promote to primary (primary or alternative) (required)

FLAGS
  --reason STRING    Audit-log reason (X-Action-Reason); REQUIRED

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            Validate without persisting (server-side X-Dry-Run). Returns the would-be response.
                       If the backend does NOT honour it, the CLI exits 6 rather than reporting a write as a preview.
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification, stored in audit log. REQUIRED.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { personId, personEmail, main:true, changed:boolean } · dry-run: { dryRun:true, wouldSetMain:{ personId, personEmail } }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 5 (HTTP 404)  Person not found / out of your tenant, or the email is not on this person → verify the address belongs to the person (\`ib person email list\`)
  exit 4 (HTTP 409)  Email already belongs to another person (globally unique) → use a different address
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Permission denied      → check auth.page.person.edit
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - Deploy-gated: needs the puminet5api /api/person/setMainPersonEmail route AND the dbo.personEmail_setMain proc; until both ship, dry-run and the write both 404.

EXAMPLES
  ib person email set-main 5351 matti.alt@example.com --reason 'primary contact changed'
  ib person email set-main 5351 matti.alt@example.com --reason preview --dry-run
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib person get matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib person get <personId> [flags]
  (also: ib person show)

DESCRIPTION
  Get a single person by personId. Global persons (ownerAsiakasId=null) are fetchable by anyone. --asiakas reads a person owned by ANOTHER company (cross-tenant; developer/admin lever) — without it the lookup is scoped to the active company and a foreign personId returns 404.
  Permissions: requires auth.page.person.read.

ARGUMENTS
  <personId> NUMBER    personId to fetch (required)

FLAGS
  --asiakas NUMBER    Read a person owned by this company (cross-tenant). Requires membership of that company, or sysadmin/developer; default = active company.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { personId, name, email, phone, roles:number[] }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (client-side)  --asiakas is not an integer >= 1, rejected locally before any request → pass a positive asiakasId (a company id) — \`ib company list\` shows the ones you can reach
  exit 5 (HTTP 404)  Person not found IN SCOPE → the id may be fine and the SCOPE wrong — these commands read the ACTIVE company only. Either the personId does not exist, or it belongs to another tenant: retry with \`--asiakas <id>\` (on \`person get\`), find them with \`ib customer person list --asiakas <id>\` or \`ib person search --my-companies\`, or switch lens with \`ib company switch <id>\`. Do NOT conclude the person does not exist and create a new one — that mints a duplicate.
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not a member of the --asiakas company → cross-tenant person reads need membership of the target company, or sysadmin/developer. Check what you can reach with \`ib company list\`.
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Permission denied      → check auth.page.person.read
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - Person reads are TENANT-SCOPED to your active company (plus global persons, ownerAsiakasId=null, and always yourself). A 404 therefore means 'not in this scope', not 'not in the database'.

SEE ALSO
  ib customer person list, ib person search

EXAMPLES
  ib person get 6233
  ib person get 6300 --asiakas 1380
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib person list matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib person list [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  List the active company's persons. By DEFAULT returns its MEMBERS (the asiakasPerson attachment — the same set as \`ib customer person list\`); --owned returns the persons it OWNS (person.ownerAsiakasId) instead. --asiakas <id> scopes to the MEMBERS of another company — you must belong to it, OR be a sysadmin/developer (who may target any tenant). Optional --role uses ROLE_NAME_BY_TYPEID from @ibetoni/constants.
  Permissions: requires auth.page.person.read.

FLAGS
  --role STRING    Filter by role name (e.g. driver, admin, laskuAdmin)
  --asiakas NUMBER    Scope to the MEMBERS of this asiakasId instead of the active company (you must belong to it, or be a sysadmin/developer). Combine with --owned for the persons it owns.
  --owned    List persons the company OWNS (person.ownerAsiakasId) instead of its asiakasPerson members (the default).
  --limit NUMBER    Max rows (capped at 500) (default: 100)

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  ListEnvelope<{ personId, name, email, roles:number[] }> (+truncated:true when the result hit the limit; backend ≥ 2026-06-11)

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (client-side)  --asiakas is not an integer >= 1, rejected locally before any request → pass a positive asiakasId (a company id) — \`ib company list\` shows the ones you can reach
  exit 4 (client-side)  --limit is not an integer >= 1, rejected locally before any request → pass a positive integer; this command caps at 500, so narrow with the company/role filters rather than raising the cap
  exit 4 (HTTP 400)  Unknown role           → use a role from @ibetoni/constants ROLE_TYPEID_BY_NAME
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Permission denied      → check auth.page.person.read
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - This command does NOT search by name — it enumerates and filters by role/company. To find a person by name or email use \`ib person search <query>\` (which also accepts \`--search\`).

SEE ALSO
  ib person search

EXAMPLES
  ib person list
  ib person list --owned
  ib person list --asiakas 1349 --limit 50
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib person log matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib person log <personId> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Change-tracker audit trail for one person — who changed what, when, with the \`--reason\` recorded by every write. INCLUDES role grants/revokes (fieldName 'asiakasPersonSetting', e.g. 'Rooli lisätty: asiakasAdmin (Asiakas Admin)'); pass \`--field asiakasPersonSetting\` to see only role changes. GET /api/changes/person/:personId/:ownerAsiakasId; owner defaults to the active company. --field filters client-side.
  Auth: requires login (any authenticated user).

ARGUMENTS
  <personId> NUMBER    personId whose audit trail to fetch (required)

FLAGS
  --owner NUMBER    ownerAsiakasId (default: active company; a non-integer value exits 4 client-side)
  --limit NUMBER    Max rows (capped at 500) (default: 100)
  --field STRING    Filter by changeTracker fieldName (e.g. asiakasPersonSetting for role changes)

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  ListEnvelope<{ changeId, field, oldValue, newValue, changeType, personId, personName, at, description, reason }> (+truncated:true when the page filled --limit — cursor-less route, so a full page may hide older rows) (+hint when --field filtered a capped page: the filter saw only the newest --limit rows)

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 4 (client-side)  --limit is not an integer >= 1, rejected locally before any request → pass a positive integer; this cursor-less route caps at 500 — raise --limit to reach older rows (\`--field\` only narrows the page you already fetched)
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not a member of that company (and not admin) → ib company switch to that owner, or use an admin token
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

EXAMPLES
  ib person log 63
  ib person log 63 --field asiakasPersonSetting
  ib person log 63 --owner 27 --limit 50
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib person me matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib person me [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Your own profile, your roles aggregated across all your companies, and the companies you can act on. Derives identity from the JWT (works with IB_TOKEN). For the roles scoped to a single company, use \`person role list --asiakas\`.
  Auth: requires login (any authenticated user).

FLAGS
  (none)

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { personId, name, email, phone, activeCompany:{asiakasId,name}, tier:'developer'|'admin'|'standard', roles:[{roleTypeId,role}], companies:[{asiakasId,name,current}], impersonating?:{actorPersonId,sessionId} } — \`tier\` is the capability/discovery gate (the MCP-reachable equivalent of \`auth whoami\`'s tier); \`impersonating\` present only when acting as another person.

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

EXAMPLES
  ib person me
  ib person me --pretty
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib person merge matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib person merge [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Merge two duplicate persons: the secondary's references (keikka / vehicle / tyomaa / asiakas / betoni / tuote) move onto the main, then the secondary is DELETED. IRREVERSIBLE and admin gated; every merge is audited server-side. --dry-run runs the read-only /validate safety check (what would move + conflicts) and NEVER merges. A real merge requires --reason.
  Permissions: requires company admin on the tenant (system admin for another owner).

FLAGS
  --main NUMBER    personId to KEEP — references merge into this one (required)
  --secondary NUMBER    personId to REMOVE — merged away then deleted (required)
  --owner NUMBER    ownerAsiakasId (default: active company; a non-integer value exits 4 client-side)
  --unowned    Merge within the UNOWNED class — BOTH persons must have ownerAsiakasId 0 or NULL (self-registrations, imports, pre-ownership rows: where duplicates actually accumulate). System admin only; mutually exclusive with --owner (fb#849)

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            CLIENT-side preview: resolves locally, no write reaches the wire (works under --read-only).
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification, stored in audit log. REQUIRED unless --dry-run (person merge is irreversible; --dry-run previews via /validate).

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  real: { success, safetyValidation, timestamp, ... } | dry-run: { dryRun: true, validation: { success, ... } }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (HTTP 400)  Validation failed (missing/equal ids, or safety check) → check --main/--secondary; run --dry-run first
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not permitted on this tenant → ib company switch to that owner, or use an admin token
  exit 5 (HTTP 404)  One or both persons not found or access denied → verify --main/--secondary and --owner
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - ALWAYS --dry-run first: the /merge route has no X-Dry-Run guard, so a real invocation merges immediately.
  - --dry-run issues a read-only POST to /validate (tagged \`read\`), so it runs even under --read-only / IB_READ_ONLY; only a real merge is blocked by the write-lock.
  - Affects keikka / vehicle / tyomaa / asiakas / betoni / tuote rows and the change history; caches are invalidated server-side; a pre-merge snapshot is written to the person combinator audit log.
  - Both persons must share one owner class: a tenant id, or (--unowned) the unowned class where owner 0 and NULL count as equal. Deploy-gated: an older backend 400s on --unowned.

SEE ALSO
  ib person duplicates, ib person delete

EXAMPLES
  ib person merge --main 6001 --secondary 6002 --dry-run
  ib person merge --main 6001 --secondary 6002 --reason 'dedupe: same phone'
  ib person merge --main 10 --secondary 27 --unowned --dry-run
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib person notify matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib person notify <person> --title <title> --body <body> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Send an FCM push to a person — ergonomic alias for \`ib notification fcm send --person <person>\`. Admin/HR-gated. <person> is a personId or a name resolved within your company. --dry-run previews recipient + device count.
  Permissions: requires company admin (isAsiakasAdmin) or HR admin (isHRAdmin) on the active company, or global sysadmin (server-enforced).

ARGUMENTS
  <person> STRING    Recipient personId, or a name resolved within your company (required)

FLAGS
  --title STRING    Notification title (required)
  --body STRING    Notification body (required)
  --data STRING    Extra FCM data payload as a JSON object

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            Validate without persisting (server-side X-Dry-Run). Returns the would-be response.
                       If the backend does NOT honour it, the CLI exits 6 rather than reporting a write as a preview.
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification. Stored in audit log.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  Same as \`ib notification fcm send\` (delegates to it).

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (HTTP 400)  Missing/invalid field (no --title/--body, ambiguous name, non-object --data) → supply --title/--body and an unambiguous person
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not Admin/HR on the active company → switch to a company where you are admin/HR
  exit 5 (HTTP 404)  Recipient not found in your company → check the personId / name
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - Thin alias — same gate, name resolution, and output as \`ib notification fcm send\`. Deploy-gated.

SEE ALSO
  ib notification fcm send

EXAMPLES
  ib person notify 6233 --title 'Keikka siirretty' --body 'Alkaa klo 8'
  ib person notify 'Juha Urho' --title Muistutus --body Tarkista --dry-run
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib person owner matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib person owner <personId> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Set or clear a person's owner company (ownerAsiakasId). Provide EXACTLY ONE of --global (make the person GLOBAL/self-managing, ownerAsiakasId=null, discoverable across companies) or --asiakas <id> (assign/move ownership). This is SEPARATE from roles — a global person can still hold roles via \`ib person role grant\`, and from membership via \`ib customer person add\`. Requires --reason.
  Permissions: requires developer/system-admin: any person → any target, self (your own personId): → null always; → a company only if you are a member of it, company-admin: may release a person CURRENTLY owned by your company → global (cannot pull others in).

ARGUMENTS
  <personId> NUMBER    personId whose owner to change (required)

FLAGS
  --global    Make the person global (ownerAsiakasId=null)
  --asiakas NUMBER    Set owner to this asiakasId
  --reason STRING    Audit-log reason (X-Action-Reason); REQUIRED

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            Validate without persisting (server-side X-Dry-Run). Returns the would-be response.
                       If the backend does NOT honour it, the CLI exits 6 rather than reporting a write as a preview.
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification, stored in audit log. REQUIRED.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { personId, ownerAsiakasId } or { dryRun: true, wouldSetOwner: { personId, from, to } }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (client-side)  --asiakas is not an integer >= 1, rejected locally before any request → pass a positive asiakasId (a company id) — \`ib company list\` shows the ones you can reach
  exit 4 (client-side)  Missing --reason       → pass --reason 'why'
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not allowed to change this person's owner → see the authz rules above (developer/self/company-admin)
  exit 5 (HTTP 404)  Person not found IN SCOPE → the id may be fine and the SCOPE wrong — these commands read the ACTIVE company only. Either the personId does not exist, or it belongs to another tenant: retry with \`--asiakas <id>\` (on \`person get\`), find them with \`ib customer person list --asiakas <id>\` or \`ib person search --my-companies\`, or switch lens with \`ib company switch <id>\`. Do NOT conclude the person does not exist and create a new one — that mints a duplicate.
  exit 4 (client-side)  Bad flags              → provide exactly one of --global / --asiakas and a --reason

EXAMPLES
  ib person owner 5351 --global --reason 'make self-managing'
  ib person owner 5351 --asiakas 26 --reason 'assign to company 26'
  ib person owner 5351 --global --reason preview --dry-run
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib person role explain matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib person role explain <name> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Explain a role NAME: its asiakasPersonSettingTypeId, human display name, the access tiers it grants (anyAdmin/anyWorker/anyViewer/laskuRead/requestOffer/adminCompanySelection), and whether it is deprecated — all from @ibetoni/constants. Enriched with the LIVE DB \`description\` (internal flag name, e.g. isAsiakasAdmin) and \`comment\` (rich Finnish text) read from GET /api/asiakasPersonSettings/getAllTypes, so the prose never drifts from dbo.asiakasPersonSettingTypes. Requires auth (any logged-in user); description/comment are null for roles the endpoint omits (soft-deleted pumppuHandler/Viewer). Use it to disambiguate the role names accepted by \`person role grant/revoke\` and \`customer person list --role\`.
  Auth: requires login (any authenticated user).

ARGUMENTS
  <name> STRING    role name (e.g. asiakasAdmin, keikkaHandler, lomaseurannassa) (required)

FLAGS
  (none)

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { role, typeId, displayName: string|null, description: string|null, comment: string|null, tiers: string[], deprecated: boolean }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (client-side)  unknown or ambiguous role name — rejected by the CLI before any request → pass an exact role name; the error names your options and \`ib person role explain <name>\` describes one. "tarjousAdmin" is not a role name — it denotes TWO (fb#418)
  exit 4 (HTTP 400)  Unknown role name      → see ROLE_TYPEID_BY_NAME in @ibetoni/constants
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

SEE ALSO
  ib person role grant, ib person role revoke, ib customer person list

EXAMPLES
  ib person role explain asiakasAdmin
  ib person role explain lomaseurannassa
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib person role grant matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib person role grant <personId> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Grant a per-company role to a person. POST /api/asiakasPersonSettings/add/:asiakasId/:personId/:roleTypeId. Admin-gated on the tenant (tier depends on the role). --dry-run previews via the backend ({ dryRun:true, wouldCreate }).
  Permissions: requires company admin on the target tenant (tier per role).

ARGUMENTS
  <personId> NUMBER    personId (required)

FLAGS
  --role STRING    Role name (REQUIRED), e.g. keikkaHandler, vehicleHandler, hrAdmin
  --asiakas NUMBER    Target asiakasId (REQUIRED)

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            Validate without persisting (server-side X-Dry-Run). Returns the would-be response.
                       If the backend does NOT honour it, the CLI exits 6 rather than reporting a write as a preview.
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification, stored in audit log. REQUIRED.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { granted: { personId, asiakasId, roleTypeId } } | { dryRun:true, wouldCreate:{ personId, asiakasId, personSettingTypeId, personSettingString }, validation }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (client-side)  unknown or ambiguous role name — rejected by the CLI before any request → pass an exact role name; the error names your options and \`ib person role explain <name>\` describes one. "tarjousAdmin" is not a role name — it denotes TWO (fb#418)
  exit 4 (client-side)  --asiakas is not an integer >= 1, rejected locally before any request → pass a positive asiakasId (a company id) — \`ib company list\` shows the ones you can reach
  exit 4 (HTTP 400)  Unknown role / company limit reached → use a name from ROLE_TYPEID_BY_NAME
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not a tenant admin     → use a system-admin token or a tenant admin
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - "TarjousAdmin" is NOT a usable --role value: the name denotes two different roles. laskupohjaAdmin (typeId 1) is what dbo.asiakasPersonSettingTypes + @ibetoni/constants call isTarjousAdmin, and is what the BetoniJerry email-recipient fallback and \`ib jerry admin detail\`.admins read; laskuAdmin (typeId 5) is what the Jerry admin dashboard's tarjousAdminCount and the Jerry validation profile's people.tarjousAdmin check read. Granting the documented one leaves Jerry validation red with a message saying you granted nothing — pass the explicit name instead (fb#418).

EXAMPLES
  ib person role grant 5351 --role keikkaHandler --asiakas 26 --reason 'onboard handler'
  ib person role grant 5351 --role vehicleHandler --asiakas 26 --reason preview --dry-run
"
`;

