exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib person role revoke matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib person role revoke <personId> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Revoke a per-company role from a person (idempotent: { removed:0 } when absent). Looks up the asiakasPersonSettingId then DELETEs it. --dry-run previews via the backend ({ dryRun:true, wouldDelete }).
  Permissions: requires company admin on the target tenant (tier per role).

ARGUMENTS
  <personId> NUMBER    personId (required)

FLAGS
  --role STRING    Role name (REQUIRED)
  --asiakas NUMBER    Target asiakasId (REQUIRED)

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            Validate without persisting (server-side X-Dry-Run). Returns the would-be response.
                       If the backend does NOT honour it, the CLI exits 6 rather than reporting a write as a preview.
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification, stored in audit log. REQUIRED.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { removed: 1 } | { removed: 0 } (absent) | { dryRun:true, wouldDelete:{ asiakasPersonSettingId }, validation }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (client-side)  unknown or ambiguous role name — rejected by the CLI before any request → pass an exact role name; the error names your options and \`ib person role explain <name>\` describes one. "tarjousAdmin" is not a role name — it denotes TWO (fb#418)
  exit 4 (client-side)  --asiakas is not an integer >= 1, rejected locally before any request → pass a positive asiakasId (a company id) — \`ib company list\` shows the ones you can reach
  exit 4 (HTTP 400)  Unknown role           → use a name from ROLE_TYPEID_BY_NAME
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not a tenant admin     → use a system-admin token or a tenant admin
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

EXAMPLES
  ib person role revoke 5351 --role keikkaHandler --asiakas 26 --reason rotation
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib person search matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib person search [<query>] [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Free-text search across person names / emails. POST /api/person/search. Scoped to your active company. Four mutually exclusive scopes: (default) the active company; --asiakas <id> one OTHER company; --my-companies every company you belong to, in one server-side call (with a per-company client-sweep fallback if that endpoint isn't deployed yet); --all-companies EVERY tenant (developer/sysadmin only). --my-companies and --all-companies return one flat list tagged with the asiakasId/name of each hit. Global persons (ownerAsiakasId=null) are included in every company's results.
  Permissions: requires auth.page.person.read, --asiakas: a company you belong to, or sysadmin/developer for any tenant, --all-companies: sysadmin/developer (server-enforced).

ARGUMENTS
  <query> STRING    search string (or pass --search) (optional)

FLAGS
  --search STRING    Search query (alias for the <query> positional)
  --limit NUMBER    Max results (default: 50)
  --asiakas NUMBER    Search this asiakasId instead of your active company (cross-tenant; any tenant for sysadmin/developer)
  --my-companies    Search across all companies you belong to; each hit carries its asiakasId/asiakasName
  --all-companies    Search EVERY tenant, no owner filter (developer/sysadmin only); each hit carries its asiakasId/asiakasName

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  ListEnvelope<{ personId, name, email, phone, asiakasId }>. With --my-companies / --all-companies each row also carries asiakasName, and the envelope gains truncated:true when the result hit the limit (backend ≥ 2026-06-11).

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 4 (client-side)  --limit is not an integer >= 1, rejected locally before any request → pass a positive integer; this is a search cap (default 50), so narrow the search term rather than raising it
  exit 4 (client-side)  --asiakas is not an integer >= 1, rejected locally before any request → pass a positive asiakasId (a company id) — \`ib company list\` shows the ones you can reach
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Permission denied (page permission, or no access to the requested scope) → check auth.page.person.read; --asiakas on another tenant and --all-companies additionally require sysadmin/developer
  exit 5 (HTTP 404)  --all-companies route not deployed on this backend → check \`ib version\`; drop --all-companies and use --asiakas <id> or --my-companies meanwhile
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - The scope flags are mutually exclusive (exit 4) — they name three different result sets, so no precedence rule is applied.
  - --all-companies is DEPLOY-GATED on GET /api/cli/person/search/global; a 404 there means the backend predates it. It has no client-side fallback on purpose: a global sweep cannot be synthesized from your own memberships, and a narrower result would read as complete.
  - --all-companies is an unindexed cross-tenant scan (IX_person_owner is a tenant-first index), so it is bounded server-side by --limit. Prefer --asiakas <id> when you know the company.

EXAMPLES
  ib person search 'Matti'
  ib person search 'Ikonen' --my-companies
  ib person search 'Jerry' --asiakas 1349
  ib person search 'Ikonen' --all-companies --limit 100
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib person update matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib person update <personId> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Update a person. Set fields with typed flags (--first/--last/--phone/--email/--memo) and/or a --body/--from-json JSON patch (typed flags win); at least one field is required. Omitted fields are PRESERVED (the backend read-merges the stored row); pass an empty string to CLEAR a field (e.g. --email ""). On Windows PowerShell a bare "" is DROPPED and the NEXT flag silently becomes the value — use the equals form \`--email=\` there, which means the same thing in bash (\`ib help shell-quoting\`). Owner changes are separate — use \`ib person owner\`. Requires --reason.
  Permissions: requires auth.page.person.edit.

ARGUMENTS
  <personId> NUMBER    personId to update (required)

FLAGS
  --first STRING    personFirstName
  --last STRING    personLastName
  --phone STRING    personPhone
  --email STRING    personEmail (pass "" to clear — PowerShell DROPS a bare "", so use \`--email=\` there (same meaning in bash; \`ib help shell-quoting\`))
  --memo STRING    personMemo — free-text note/comment
  --body JSON    Patch body (JSON), merged UNDER the typed flags. Mutually exclusive with --from-json. ⚠ Windows PowerShell splits this argument on its inner double-quotes, so inline JSON arrives mangled and exits 4 as a too-many-arguments usage error — use --from-json <file|-> there, or typed flags (fb#437; see \`ib help shell-quoting\`).
  --from-json STRING    Read the patch body from a file (or - for stdin); shell-safe alternative to --body. Mutually exclusive with --body.
  --reason STRING    Audit-log reason (X-Action-Reason); REQUIRED

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            Validate without persisting (server-side X-Dry-Run). Returns the would-be response.
                       If the backend does NOT honour it, the CLI exits 6 rather than reporting a write as a preview.
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification, stored in audit log. REQUIRED.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { ok: true, updated: { personId } } or { dryRun: true, wouldUpdate: { personId, ... } }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (client-side)  No fields to update    → pass at least one typed flag (--first/--last/--phone/--email/--memo) or a --body/--from-json patch
  exit 5 (HTTP 404)  Person not found IN SCOPE → the id may be fine and the SCOPE wrong — these commands read the ACTIVE company only. Either the personId does not exist, or it belongs to another tenant: retry with \`--asiakas <id>\` (on \`person get\`), find them with \`ib customer person list --asiakas <id>\` or \`ib person search --my-companies\`, or switch lens with \`ib company switch <id>\`. Do NOT conclude the person does not exist and create a new one — that mints a duplicate.
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Permission denied      → check auth.page.person.edit
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - Prefer typed flags for the common contact fields — --email/--phone map to personEmail/personPhone. Use --body/--from-json for columns without a typed flag.
  - On Windows PowerShell inline --body JSON often fails (the shell strips the inner double-quotes, so the CLI sees e.g. {personEmail:x} unquoted) — use typed flags, or pass --from-json <file|-> (a file, or - for stdin) to avoid shell quoting entirely.

EXAMPLES
  ib person update 6268 --email jussi@ariem.fi --phone 0405164758 --reason "onboarding contact details"
  ib person update 5351 --phone "+358501234567" --reason "phone change"
  ib person update 5351 --email "" --reason "clear email"
  ib person update 5351 --body '{"personPhone":"+358501234567"}' --reason "phone change"
  ib person update 5351 --from-json ./patch.json --reason "phone change"
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib reference detail delete matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib reference detail delete <command...> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Delete one command-catalog row by its exact key — prunes orphans of re-homed/removed commands (developer only)
  Auth: requires login (any authenticated user).

ARGUMENTS
  <command...> STRING    The exact stored command key after \`ib\` (e.g. ai conversation). Unlike get/set this is NOT validated against the live catalogue — that is precisely what lets you remove an orphan whose command no longer exists. (required)

FLAGS
  (none)

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            Validate without persisting (server-side X-Dry-Run). Returns the would-be response.
                       If the backend does NOT honour it, the CLI exits 6 rather than reporting a write as a preview.
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification, stored in audit log. REQUIRED unless --dry-run.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { deleted } (rows removed, 0 or 1 — idempotent) | --dry-run: { dryRun:true, wouldDelete:{ command, exists }, validation }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not a developer        → Requires isDeveloper / isSystemAdmin (server-enforced)
  exit 4 (client-side)  Missing --reason on a real delete, or empty command path → Pass --reason (or --dry-run to preview) and a command path

EXAMPLES
  ib reference detail delete ai conversation --dry-run
  ib reference detail delete ai conversation --reason 'orphan: ai domain re-homed under dev'
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib reference detail get matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib reference detail get <command...> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  On-demand business/AI context for one command (DB-backed via /api/cli/command-catalog); exit 5 if none
  Auth: requires login (any authenticated user).

ARGUMENTS
  <command...> STRING    Command path after \`ib\` (e.g. keikka latest) (required)

FLAGS
  (none)

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { command, summary, detail, hint }. exit 5 when unknown or no detail yet.

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 5 (client-side)  Unknown command (client-side guard) → \`ib commands\` / \`ib reference dump\` for valid paths; or \`<cmd> --help\`
  exit 5 (HTTP 404)  Known command, but no detail recorded yet → no business-context detail is recorded for this command yet — fall back to \`<cmd> --help\`, which is self-contained; a developer can fill the catalog entry

EXAMPLES
  ib reference detail get keikka latest
  ib reference detail get jerry check-address
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib reference detail lint matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib reference detail lint [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Audit the command-catalog for orphan rows — keys with no live command (re-homed/renamed leftovers); --strict for CI (developer only)
  Auth: requires login (any authenticated user).

FLAGS
  --strict    Exit 1 if any orphan row exists (for CI)

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { items: [{ command, severity:'warn', kind:'orphan', summary, hint }], count } — one finding per catalog key with no live command

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 1 (client-side)  --strict and orphan rows found → Prune each with \`ib reference detail delete <key> --reason <r>\`, or seed the re-homed command
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not a developer        → Requires isDeveloper / isSystemAdmin (server-enforced)

NOTES
  - Read-only: one GET of the whole catalog plus a local diff against the live command specs. The class behind fb#73 (\`ib customer prh\` re-homed to \`ib opendata prh\`).

SEE ALSO
  ib reference detail delete, ib reference detail list

EXAMPLES
  ib reference detail lint
  ib reference detail lint --strict
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib reference detail list matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib reference detail list [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  List command-catalog entries, optionally ordered by stalest (DB-backed)
  Auth: requires login (any authenticated user).

FLAGS
  --stalest NUMBER    Return up to N entries sorted by least-recently reviewed
  --domain STRING    Only commands in this ib domain (e.g. attachment) — narrows BEFORE --stalest, so the budget isn't spent on unrelated commands
  --with-detail    Include each entry's full detail text (adds a \`detail\` field per item), folding the per-command \`reference detail get\` into this one call. Needs the backend deployed; on an old backend the field is simply absent.
  --needs-review    Only rows still needing grooming: aiConfidence below the threshold (or unassessed) AND not parked, oldest-first.
  --max-confidence NUMBER    Threshold for --needs-review (default 90).
  --search STRING    Only rows whose command PATH contains this substring (case-insensitive). Client-side, so it works without a raw DB LIKE — the discover half of \`reference detail delete\`.
  --orphans    Only ORPHAN rows: keys whose command no longer exists in the live catalogue (re-homed/renamed leftovers). Same set as \`reference detail lint\`, but streamed as normal list rows so you can pipe → \`delete\`. Compose with --search to narrow.
  --limit NUMBER    Return at most N rows. A client-side payload CAP applied LAST (after --search/--orphans), not a pager — there is no cursor, so the rows past N are simply not returned and \`truncated: true\` says so.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { items: [{ command, summary, lastReviewed, runs, aiConfidence, needsHumanReview, detail? }], count, truncated? } — \`detail\` present only with --with-detail. --search/--orphans filter client-side and recompute count; \`truncated: true\` appears only when --limit actually cut rows.

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 2 (client-side)  Not authenticated      → Run \`ib auth login\`
  exit 4 (client-side)  Unknown --domain       → \`ib commands\` for valid domains
  exit 4 (client-side)  --limit / --stalest is not an integer >= 1 → pass a positive integer; a bad cap is rejected rather than dropped, which would silently return the WHOLE catalog

NOTES
  - --search and --orphans are client-side post-filters (no backend deploy needed): the full catalog is fetched, then narrowed locally.
  - NARROWING, not paging, is the model here: the backend returns the whole catalog in one shot and there is no cursor. Reach for --domain/--search/--needs-review/--stalest to ask a smaller question; --limit only caps the payload you get back (useful against --with-detail, which is ~154 large rows).
  - --stalest and --limit are different caps: --stalest caps the SERVER page and orders it least-recently-reviewed first, --limit caps client-side AFTER the filters. Passing both gives you at most --limit of the stalest --stalest.
  - Because --stalest caps the server page first, run --orphans WITHOUT --stalest for a full-catalog orphan scan (with --stalest it only scans that page).
  - --orphans returns the same set as \`reference detail lint\` but as plain list rows, so \`reference detail list --orphans\` → \`reference detail delete <key>\` is a self-contained discover→prune workflow for an MCP/exec-only caller.

EXAMPLES
  ib reference detail list
  ib reference detail list --stalest 20
  ib reference detail list --stalest 10 --domain attachment
  ib reference detail list --stalest 10 --domain attachment --with-detail
  ib reference detail list --needs-review --max-confidence 90
  ib reference detail list --search 'dev bug'
  ib reference detail list --orphans
  ib reference detail list --with-detail --limit 20
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib reference detail set matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib reference detail set <command...> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Write summary and/or detail for one command in the command-catalog (developer only)
  Auth: requires login (any authenticated user).

ARGUMENTS
  <command...> STRING    Command path after \`ib\` (e.g. keikka latest) (required)

FLAGS
  --summary STRING    Short one-line summary stored in the catalog (≤160 chars, server-enforced)
  --detail STRING    Full markdown business-context detail (≤2000 chars, server-enforced). Don't recap flags/exit codes — those already render in \`--help\` from the spec; spend the budget on business context only found here.
  --ai-confidence NUMBER    Self-assessed completeness/correctness 0–100 (groom rubric). Omit on a human edit to reset the score.
  --needs-human-review    Park the row for a human (excludes it from --needs-review); set with a low --ai-confidence when blocked.
  --field STRING    Edit-mode target field: summary | detail (default detail)
  --replace STRING    Edit mode: replace this literal text in the target field (exactly once unless --all)
  --with STRING    Replacement for --replace (empty deletes the matched text; pass "" to clear — PowerShell DROPS a bare "", so use \`--with=\` there (same meaning in bash; \`ib help shell-quoting\`))
  --append STRING    Edit mode: append text to the target field (verbatim)
  --prepend STRING    Edit mode: prepend text to the target field (verbatim)
  --all    With --replace: substitute every occurrence
  --from-json STRING    Read the content fields from a JSON object file (or - for stdin); argv-safe route for prose containing Finnish ä/ö or an em-dash. Accepts summary, detail, aiConfidence, field, replace, with, append, prepend. Explicit flags outrank the file; unknown or wrong-typed keys exit 4.

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            Validate without persisting (server-side X-Dry-Run). Returns the would-be response.
                       If the backend does NOT honour it, the CLI exits 6 rather than reporting a write as a preview.
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification. Stored in audit log.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { command, runs, … } (backend response) | plain --dry-run: {dryRun:true, wouldSave:{command, exists, writes:{summaryChars?, detailChars?}, aiConfidence, needsHumanReview}, validation} | edit-mode --dry-run: {dryRun:true, command, field, matchCount?, addedLines, removedLines, sameContent, unified}

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 5 (client-side)  Unknown command        → \`ib commands\` for valid paths
  exit 4 (HTTP 400)  summary >160 or detail >2000 chars (the message names the submitted length) → Trim to the cap — cut any flag/exit-code recap first (it already renders in \`--help\`), keep the business context

NOTES
  - --dry-run has two resolutions. EDIT mode (--replace/--append/--prepend) resolves CLIENT-side and never PUTs — safe on any backend. A plain --summary/--detail --dry-run is SERVER-side (X-Dry-Run) and DEPLOY-GATED: the PUT handler ignored the header until puminet5api shipped the wouldSave branch, so against an older backend a plain --dry-run WRITES FOR REAL and overwrites the entry (fb#286). Until that backend deploys, preview a full-field rewrite with \`reference detail get\` first, or use edit mode.
  - Caps are validated BEFORE the dry-run branch, so an over-cap payload still exits 4 under --dry-run rather than reporting a would-be write.
  - The save proc COALESCEs the CONTENT fields — an omitted --summary/--detail keeps its current value (pass "" to clear — PowerShell DROPS a bare "", so use \`--summary=\` there (same meaning in bash; \`ib help shell-quoting\`)), which is why the dry-run's \`writes\` lists only the fields you sent. aiConfidence/needsHumanReview are DIRECT-assigned: omitting them RESETS the score and un-parks the row for the grooming routine.
  - PASS PROSE VIA --from-json, NOT argv, whenever it contains a non-ASCII character (fb#613). Windows PowerShell reinterprets UTF-8 native arguments as latin1, so \`Ylijäämäbetonin\` is stored as \`YlijÃ¤Ã¤mÃ¤betonin\` while the call exits 0 and echoes a success payload. The corruption is invisible here in a way it is not elsewhere: this catalog is served to AI agents as authoritative, lives outside git, and nothing diffs or lints it. --needs-human-review and --all take no value, so they stay on argv alongside --from-json and are deliberately NOT accepted as JSON keys.

EXAMPLES
  ib reference detail set keikka list --summary 'Lists delivery orders' --reason 'initial fill'
  ib reference detail set keikka list --detail '## Keikka list\\nReturns ...' --reason 'update'
  ib reference detail set keikka list --replace '14 latest' --with '20 latest' --reason 'fix count' --dry-run
  ib reference detail set sijainti types --from-json ./detail.json --reason 'refresh catalog'
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib reference dump matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib reference dump [<domain...>] [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Emit the full command surface as JSON for one-shot AI ingestion. The universal 401/500 error contract is hoisted to a single top-level \`commonErrors\` block and stripped from each spec (it applied to every command) — read \`commonErrors\` together with each spec's command-specific \`errors\`. Flag/error rows repeated verbatim across many commands are likewise stored ONCE in top-level \`sharedFlags\`/\`sharedErrors\`: an "@id" string inside a spec's \`flags\`/\`errors\` array resolves to the row under that id (e.g. "@reason" -> sharedFlags.reason). Pass one or more domains (the token after \`ib\`, e.g. keikka) to narrow the commands map — STRONGLY preferred over the full surface (a one-domain dump is a fraction of the bytes). The full (no-domain) dump carries a \`notice\` field pointing this out. \`glossary\` (the term+synonyms vocabulary index) is OPT-IN via \`--glossary\`. \`--commands-only\` emits just { version, generatedAt, commonErrors, sharedFlags, sharedErrors, commands } for callers that already know the domain.
  Auth: none (public).

ARGUMENTS
  <domain...> STRING    Restrict the commands map to one or more domains (the token after \`ib\`, e.g. keikka). Multiple domains share a single primer. Unknown domain exits 4 listing valid domains. (optional)

FLAGS
  --glossary    Include the term+synonyms vocabulary INDEX (fetched from the DB) under \`glossary\`. Off by default to keep the dump small; fetch definitions on demand with \`ib glossary lookup <term>\` / \`ib glossary list\`.
  --commands-only    Emit only { version, generatedAt, commonErrors, commands } — drop the overview/topics/feedbackGuidance primer and skip the glossary fetch (no token needed). Fewer bytes per dump.
  --lean    Drop each command's \`notes\`/\`seeAlso\` prose (KEEPS \`examples\`) — ~25k fewer tokens on the full surface. For a whole-surface scan you get what exists + how to call it; fetch the dropped caveats/cross-refs per-command via \`ib <command> --help\`. Composes with --commands-only and domain filters.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { version, generatedAt, commonErrors: CommandError[], sharedFlags: { id: CommandFlag }, sharedErrors: { id: CommandError }, notice?, overview, glossary, feedbackGuidance, topics, commands: { '<command>': CommandSpec } } — with --commands-only: { version, generatedAt, commonErrors, sharedFlags, sharedErrors, commands }; with --lean each spec drops notes/seeAlso (examples kept). \`commonErrors\` (401/500) applies to EVERY command and is omitted from each spec's \`errors\`. A spec's \`flags\`/\`errors\` array may contain "@id" reference STRINGS — resolve each in sharedFlags/sharedErrors (rows repeated across many commands, stored once). \`notice\` appears only on the full (no-domain) dump. \`glossary\` is the term+synonyms INDEX only and is EMPTY unless \`--glossary\` is passed; fetch a definition with \`ib glossary lookup <term>\` or all of them with \`ib glossary list\`.

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (client-side)  Unknown domain         → run \`ib commands\` (no arg) to see valid domains
  exit 1 (client-side)  I/O error              → retry; check stdout pipe

EXAMPLES
  ib reference dump keikka
  ib reference dump --lean --commands-only
  ib reference dump --glossary
  ib reference dump | jq .commonErrors
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib sales customer list matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib sales customer list [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Companies genuinely running work through betoni.online — those with their own keikka rows. NOT the same as 'has logged in' (59 companies have a login, 2 have keikkaa). lastLoginOwn excludes PumiNet Oy staff, who hold membership in many tenants; lastLoginAny is kept alongside so the difference is inspectable.
  Permissions: requires isSystemAdmin.

FLAGS
  (none)

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  ListEnvelope<{ asiakasId, asiakasNimi, ytunnus, entryTime, lastActiveTime, keikat, firstKeikkaTime, lastKeikkaTime, vehicles, persons, lastLoginAny, lastLoginOwn }>

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not a system admin     → log in as a system admin

EXAMPLES
  ib sales customer list --pretty
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib sales prospect add matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib sales prospect add [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Add a company to the SaaS sales pipeline. --asiakas for a company already in betoni.online (companyName is backfilled from the asiakas row); --name for a COLD company with no asiakas row — which is the whole reason this pipeline has its own table.
  Permissions: requires isSystemAdmin.

FLAGS
  --asiakas NUMBER    Existing betoni.online asiakasId
  --name STRING    Company name for a cold prospect (no asiakas row)
  --ytunnus STRING    Finnish business id
  --segment STRING    pumppu | betoni | all | muu
  --tier NUMBER    1 | 2 | 3
  --region STRING    Operating area (toimialue)

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            Validate without persisting (server-side X-Dry-Run). Returns the would-be response.
                       If the backend does NOT honour it, the CLI exits 6 rather than reporting a write as a preview.
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification. Stored in audit log.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { saasProspectId }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (client-side)  Neither --asiakas nor --name given → pass one of them
  exit 4 (HTTP 400)  Prospect already exists for this company → \`ib sales prospect get --asiakas <id>\`
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not a system admin     → log in as a system admin

EXAMPLES
  ib sales prospect add --asiakas 27 --segment pumppu --tier 1 --reason "seed"
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib sales prospect get matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib sales prospect get <saasProspectId> [flags]
  (also: ib sales prospect show)

DESCRIPTION
  One SaaS prospect, by saasProspectId, --asiakas or --ytunnus. Exits 4 (not a guess) when more than one row matches the reference, and 5 when none does.
  Permissions: requires isSystemAdmin.

ARGUMENTS
  <saasProspectId> NUMBER    the row id (optional if --asiakas/--ytunnus given) (required)

FLAGS
  --asiakas NUMBER    Look up by betoni.online asiakasId
  --ytunnus STRING    Look up by Finnish business id

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { saasProspectId, asiakasId, companyName, status, analysis, … }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (client-side)  No reference given, or ambiguous match → pass the saasProspectId
  exit 5 (client-side)  No prospect matches    → \`ib sales prospect list --search <name>\`

EXAMPLES
  ib sales prospect get --asiakas 27
  ib sales prospect get --ytunnus 1869376-5 --pretty
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib sales prospect list matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib sales prospect list [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  List the betoni.online SaaS sales pipeline (dbo.saasProspect) — companies we are selling betoni.online ITSELF to. Distinct from \`ib jerry admin onboarding list\`, the BetoniJerry provider pipeline: a company sits in both at independent stages. Every filter is applied CLIENT-SIDE (the route takes no query params by design). Use --brief to drop the two long narrative columns.
  Permissions: requires isSystemAdmin.

FLAGS
  --status STRING    ei_aloitettu | analysoitu | kontaktoitu | tapaaminen | tarjous | voitettu | havitty | ei_sovellu
  --tier NUMBER    1 priority · 2 secondary · 3 long tail
  --segment STRING    pumppu | betoni | all | muu. SAME semantics as the Myynti UI buckets (fb#817): pumppu/betoni mean value-OR-all, muu means value-OR-unset (the not-yet-typed bucket). Any other value is an exact match.
  --search STRING    Case-insensitive substring over companyName + asiakasNimi + ytunnus + region (union of the Myynti UI's fields and this command's, fb#817)
  --brief    Omit analysis + pitchAngle — the full list is ~60 KB of narrative

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  ListEnvelope<{ saasProspectId, asiakasId, companyName, ytunnus, status, tier, segment, region, fleetPumps, staffCount, revenueEur, revenueYear, currentSystem, fitScore, analysis, pitchAngle, parked, jerryStatus, analysisUpdatedTime, … }>

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not a system admin     → log in as a system admin

EXAMPLES
  ib sales prospect list --brief --pretty
  ib sales prospect list --segment pumppu --status ei_aloitettu
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib sales prospect update matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib sales prospect update <saasProspectId> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Write company FACTS onto a SaaS prospect — the weekly suomen-betonipumppausyritykset task's write path. Only facts: the backend DROPS status/tier/notes/parkedUntil arriving here, because a human owns pipeline state and the task must never revert it. --fit-score and --pitch are FIRST-FILL: written only while the stored value is NULL, so a human's answer always wins. Stamps analysisUpdatedTime.
  Permissions: requires isSystemAdmin.

ARGUMENTS
  <saasProspectId> NUMBER    the row id (optional if --asiakas/--ytunnus given) (required)

FLAGS
  --asiakas NUMBER    Resolve the row by asiakasId instead of the positional id
  --ytunnus STRING    Resolve the row by business id
  --name STRING    Company name
  --segment STRING    pumppu | betoni | all | muu
  --region STRING    Operating area
  --fleet-pumps NUMBER    Pump trucks
  --staff NUMBER    Employee count
  --revenue NUMBER    Revenue in EUR
  --revenue-year NUMBER    Which year the revenue figure is from
  --current-system STRING    Excel | Google Sheets | kilpailija | oma | ei tiedossa
  --analysis STRING    Narrative analysis (markdown). Long prose — use --from-json on Windows.
  --fit-score NUMBER    1..5. FIRST-FILL only.
  --pitch STRING    How to market to this company. FIRST-FILL only.
  --body STRING    Inline JSON object of the same fields. Mutually exclusive with --from-json.
  --from-json STRING    Read the fields from a JSON file (or - for stdin). The shell-safe route for long Finnish prose: PowerShell splits an argument on its inner double quotes and silently expands backticks. Use a FILE, not a pipe, for anything containing a backslash. Typed flags win over the document.

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            Validate without persisting (server-side X-Dry-Run). Returns the would-be response.
                       If the backend does NOT honour it, the CLI exits 6 rather than reporting a write as a preview.
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification. Stored in audit log.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { success: true, fieldsWritten }  — fieldsWritten is 0 when every key in the payload fell outside the scope's whitelist, so nothing was actually written

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (client-side)  No reference given, or ambiguous match → pass the saasProspectId
  exit 5 (client-side)  No prospect matches    → \`ib sales prospect add\` first
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not a system admin     → log in as a system admin

EXAMPLES
  ib sales prospect update --asiakas 27 --fleet-pumps 27 --staff 70 --reason "weekly registry sync"
  ib sales prospect update 12 --from-json ./analysis.json --reason "weekly registry sync"
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib schedule day matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib schedule day <date> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  List keikkas for a specific day.
  Permissions: requires auth.page.grid.tilaus.read.
  Timezone: dates interpreted in active company timezone (Europe/Helsinki).

ARGUMENTS
  <date> DATE    date (YYYY-MM-DD or today/yesterday/tomorrow) (required)

FLAGS
  (none)

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  ListEnvelope<{ keikkaId, pvm, asiakasId, tyomaaId, vehicleId, tila, m3, time }> & { scope: { asiakasId } }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Permission denied      → check auth.page.grid.tilaus.read
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - Scoped to the ACTIVE company only — the echoed \`scope.asiakasId\` names which tenant was queried, so a 0-row result reads as "none in THIS company", not "none scheduled anywhere". For a cross-tenant rollup, use \`ib stats --all\` instead (a different aggregate shape, not a keikka list).

SEE ALSO
  ib stats

EXAMPLES
  ib schedule day 2026-06-01
  ib schedule day tomorrow
"
`;

