exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib vehicle update matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib vehicle update <vehicleId> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Update a vehicle (read-merge-write: only provided flags change; others preserved). POST /api/vehicle/save.
  Permissions: requires auth.page.vehicle.edit.
  Timezone: dates interpreted in active company timezone (Europe/Helsinki).

ARGUMENTS
  <vehicleId> NUMBER    vehicleId to update (required)

FLAGS
  --reg STRING    Registration number
  --name STRING    Display name
  --no NUMBER    Fleet number
  --type NUMBER    vehicleTypeId
  --memo STRING    Free-text memo
  --capacity NUMBER    Concrete capacity in m3
  --puomi NUMBER    Boom length in metres (vehiclePuomi — informational; BetoniJerry matching uses sijainti puomiMin/puomiMax since 2026-07)
  --asiakas NUMBER    Owning asiakasId
  --show-in-grid    Whether the vehicle appears in the grid (true/false)
  --first-date DATE    Start of validity window (firstDate); YYYY-MM-DD or today/yesterday/tomorrow
  --last-date DATE    End of validity window (lastDate); YYYY-MM-DD or today/yesterday/tomorrow

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            CLIENT-side preview: resolves locally, no write reaches the wire (works under --read-only).
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification. Stored in audit log.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  On write: the saved vehicle record. With --dry-run: { dryRun: true, vehicleId, wouldChange: { field: { from, to } } } — the field-level diff, computed client-side without POSTing (the save route ignores X-Dry-Run, so the preview cannot persist).

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (client-side)  --asiakas is not an integer >= 1, rejected locally before any request → pass a positive asiakasId (a company id) — \`ib company list\` shows the ones you can reach
  exit 5 (HTTP 404)  Vehicle not found      → verify vehicleId
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Permission denied      → check auth.page.vehicle.edit
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

EXAMPLES
  ib vehicle update 70 --capacity 8 --reason 'remeasured'
  ib vehicle update 70 --show-in-grid false --dry-run
  ib vehicle update 70 --last-date 2026-12-31 --reason 'retiring'
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib vehicle visits matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib vehicle visits <filterType> <id> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  The active company's own vehicles that visited a worksite (tyomaa) or location (sijainti), grouped into visits with arrival/departure/duration (snapshot-based). Results are filtered to the caller's own fleet — other tenants' vehicles at a shared sijainti are not returned; a tyomaa must belong to the active company (else 404).
  Permissions: requires auth.page.vehicle.read.
  Timezone: dates interpreted in active company timezone (Europe/Helsinki).

ARGUMENTS
  <filterType> STRING    'tyomaa' or 'sijainti' (required)
  <id> NUMBER    tyomaaId or sijaintiId (required)

FLAGS
  --days NUMBER    Look-back window in days (omit for all-time)
  --date DATE    Only visits on this day (YYYY-MM-DD or today/yesterday/tomorrow; Europe/Helsinki). Filtered client-side; auto-bounds the look-back when --days is omitted

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  ListEnvelope<{ vehicleId, plate, objectName, arrived, departed, durationMin }> & { gpsAvailable }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (client-side)  Invalid filterType     → use tyomaa or sijainti
  exit 4 (client-side)  Bad --date             → YYYY-MM-DD or today/yesterday/tomorrow
  exit 5 (HTTP 404)  tyomaa not found / not owned → verify tyomaaId belongs to the active company
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Permission denied      → check auth.page.vehicle.read
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - filterType and id are POSITIONAL (\`visits sijainti 60\`), not flags — there is no --sijainti/--tyomaa option.
  - Resolving a sijaintiId by name: supplier plants belong to OTHER companies, so use \`ib sijainti list --search <name> --all\` (plain \`sijainti list\` hides them). Alternatively \`ib vehicle timeline <vehicleId> --date <d>\` labels each stop with its sijaintiId/tyomaaId.

SEE ALSO
  ib sijainti list, ib vehicle timeline

EXAMPLES
  ib vehicle visits tyomaa 17 --days 30
  ib vehicle visits sijainti 3
  ib vehicle visits sijainti 60 --date 2026-04-15
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib version matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib version [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Show the local CLI version AND the deployed iB version at the active endpoint (server commit SHA + slot). Unauthenticated — works logged out, against any --endpoint. The whole deployable iB surface (the /api/cli routes + the vendored CLI) ships inside puminet5api, so the server \`commit\` is the single source of truth for which build is live; it changes on every deployed commit, letting you tell staging from prod without manual version bumps.
  Auth: none (public).

FLAGS
  --endpoint URL    Which deployment to query (global flag) (default: active profile, else https://api.ibetoni.fi)

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { cli, endpoint, reachable, server: { app, version, commit, release, slot } | null, error? }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 7 (client-side)  Endpoint unreachable   → check --endpoint / network; the report (cli version + error) still prints

EXAMPLES
  ib version
  ib version --endpoint https://api.ibetoni.fi
  ib version --endpoint https://api-staging.ibetoni.fi
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib worksite create matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib worksite create [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Create a new worksite via POST /api/tyomaa/new. Body forwarded verbatim.
  Permissions: requires auth.page.tyomaa.edit.

FLAGS
  --body JSON    JSON object with the new tyomaa fields

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            Validate without persisting (server-side X-Dry-Run). Returns the would-be response.
                       If the backend does NOT honour it, the CLI exits 6 rather than reporting a write as a preview.
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification. Stored in audit log.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { tyomaaId, ... } (raw backend response)

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (HTTP 400)  Validation failed      → fix --body fields
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Permission denied      → check auth.page.tyomaa.edit
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

EXAMPLES
  ib worksite create --body '{"name":"Site A","address":"Main St 1","asiakasId":1349}'
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib worksite dashboard matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib worksite dashboard [<tyomaaId>] [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  One-shot Address Information Dashboard report for a worksite (tyomaa) — merges weather, building, cadastral parcel, nearby traffic cameras, nearby sijainnit, worksite deliveries, and nearby vehicles into a single JSON, with each section independently degrading to forbidden/error instead of failing the whole report. Resolve the point from EXACTLY ONE of the positional tyomaaId or --address.
  Auth: requires login (any authenticated user).

ARGUMENTS
  <tyomaaId> NUMBER    tyomaaId to report on (mutually exclusive with --address) (optional)

FLAGS
  --address STRING    Street address to resolve the point from, instead of tyomaaId (mutually exclusive)

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { point:{lat,lng}|null, address:string|null, weather, building, parcel, cameras, sijainti, deliveries, vehicles } — each section is { status:'ok'|'empty'|'forbidden'|'error', data?, error? }; a forbidden/error section never fails the whole command

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (client-side)  Missing or ambiguous point input → pass exactly one of <tyomaaId> or --address
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - Per-section gating mirrors the FE dashboard: weather/cameras/vehicles degrade to forbidden when the company module is off; building/parcel are open to any authenticated user; a bad address or unresolvable point degrades EVERY section to error instead of failing the command.
  - \`deliveries\` reports worksite delivery volume — tyomaaId-scoped when invoked by <tyomaaId>, or the nearest owned worksite at the geocoded point when invoked via --address; \`vehicles\` reports nearby BetoniJerry ecofleet vehicles; \`sijainti\` reports sijainnit found NEARBY the resolved point (~2 km).

SEE ALSO
  ib sijainti dashboard, ib opendata building, ib opendata parcel, ib worksite get

EXAMPLES
  ib worksite dashboard 1234
  ib worksite dashboard --address "Oraspolku 2, Helsinki"
"
`;

