exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib worksite log matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib worksite log <tyomaaId> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Change-tracker audit trail for one worksite (tyomaa) — who changed which field, when, old→new, with --reason. Alias of \`ib log entity tyomaa\`. GET /api/changes/tyomaa/:tyomaaId/:ownerAsiakasId.
  Auth: requires login (any authenticated user).

ARGUMENTS
  <tyomaaId> NUMBER    tyomaaId (required)

FLAGS
  --owner NUMBER    ownerAsiakasId (default: active company; a non-integer value exits 4 client-side)
  --limit NUMBER    Max rows (capped at 500) (default: 100)
  --field STRING    Filter by fieldName

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  ListEnvelope<{ changeId, entityType, entityId, field, oldValue, newValue, changeType, personId, personName, at, description, reason, impersonatedByPersonName }> (+truncated:true when the page filled --limit — cursor-less route, so a full page may hide older rows) (+hint when --field filtered a capped page: the filter saw only the newest --limit rows)

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 4 (client-side)  --limit is not an integer >= 1, rejected locally before any request → pass a positive integer; this cursor-less route caps at 500 — raise --limit to reach older rows (\`--field\` only narrows the page you already fetched)
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not a member of that company (and not admin) → ib company switch to that owner, or use an admin token
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

SEE ALSO
  ib log entity

EXAMPLES
  ib worksite log 7
"
`;

exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib worksite merge matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib worksite merge [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Merge two duplicate worksites: the secondary's references (keikka / person / grid) move onto the main, then the secondary is DELETED. IRREVERSIBLE and admin gated. --dry-run runs the read-only /validate safety check (what would move + conflicts) and NEVER merges. A real merge requires --reason.
  Permissions: requires company admin on the tenant (system admin for another owner).

FLAGS
  --main NUMBER    tyomaaId to KEEP — references merge into this one (required)
  --secondary NUMBER    tyomaaId to REMOVE — merged away then deleted (required)
  --owner NUMBER    ownerAsiakasId (default: active company; a non-integer value exits 4 client-side)

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            CLIENT-side preview: resolves locally, no write reaches the wire (works under --read-only).
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification, stored in audit log. REQUIRED unless --dry-run (worksite merge is irreversible; --dry-run previews via /validate).

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  real: { success, safetyValidation, timestamp, ... } | dry-run: { dryRun: true, validation: { success, ... } }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (HTTP 400)  Validation failed (missing/equal ids, or safety check) → check --main/--secondary; run --dry-run first
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Not permitted on this tenant → ib company switch to that owner, or use an admin token
  exit 5 (HTTP 404)  One or both worksites not found or access denied → verify --main/--secondary and --owner
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - ALWAYS --dry-run first: the /merge route has no X-Dry-Run guard, so a real invocation merges immediately.
  - --dry-run issues a read-only POST to /validate (tagged \`read\`), so it runs even under --read-only / IB_READ_ONLY; only a real merge is blocked by the write-lock.
  - Affects keikka / person / grid rows and the change history; caches are invalidated server-side.

SEE ALSO
  ib worksite duplicates, ib worksite delete

EXAMPLES
  ib worksite merge --main 701 --secondary 702 --dry-run
  ib worksite merge --main 701 --secondary 702 --reason 'dedupe: same address'
"
`;

