exports[`Help snapshots — contract stability > help for ib worksite update matches snapshot 1`] = `
"USAGE
  ib worksite update <tyomaaId> [flags]

DESCRIPTION
  Update a worksite via POST /api/tyomaa/set (ownerAsiakasId derived from the session JWT; yyyymmdd defaults to today). Set fields with typed flags (--name/--num/--address/--address2/--postal-code/--city/--driving-instructions/--comment/--invoice-ref/--contact-person) and/or a --body/--from-json JSON patch with backend column names (typed flags win); at least one field is required. Omitted fields are PRESERVED (the backend read-merges the stored row); pass an empty string to CLEAR a field (e.g. --comment ""). On Windows PowerShell a bare "" is DROPPED and the NEXT flag silently becomes the value — use the equals form \`--comment=\` there, which means the same thing in bash (\`ib help shell-quoting\`).
  Permissions: requires auth.page.tyomaa.edit.
  Timezone: dates interpreted in active company timezone (Europe/Helsinki).

ARGUMENTS
  <tyomaaId> NUMBER    tyomaaId to update (required)

FLAGS
  --name STRING    Worksite name (tyomaaNimi)
  --num STRING    Worksite number (tyomaaNum)
  --address STRING    Street address (tyomaaOsoite1)
  --address2 STRING    Address line 2 (tyomaaOsoite2)
  --postal-code STRING    Postal code (tyomaaOsoite3)
  --city STRING    City (tyomaaOsoite4)
  --driving-instructions STRING    Driving instructions (tyomaaAjoOhje)
  --comment STRING    Free-text memo (tyomaaMemo; pass "" to clear — PowerShell DROPS a bare "", so use \`--comment=\` there (same meaning in bash; \`ib help shell-quoting\`))
  --invoice-ref STRING    Invoice reference (laskuViite)
  --contact-person NUMBER    Contact personId (tyomaaContactPersonId; 0 = none)
  --body JSON    Patch body (JSON, backend column names e.g. tyomaaMemo — NOT the camelCase read keys), merged UNDER the typed flags. Mutually exclusive with --from-json.
  --from-json STRING    Read the patch body from a file (or - for stdin); shell-safe alternative to --body. Mutually exclusive with --body.
  --yyyymmdd DATE    Effective date segment YYYYMMDD (defaults to today) (default: today)

WRITE-SAFETY FLAGS
  --dry-run            Validate without persisting (server-side X-Dry-Run). Returns the would-be response.
                       If the backend does NOT honour it, the CLI exits 6 rather than reporting a write as a preview.
  --idempotency-key K  Replay protection. Cached for 24h.
  --reason TEXT        Free-text justification. Stored in audit log.

GLOBAL FLAGS
  --endpoint URL  --request-id ID  --quiet  --verbose  --pretty  --json  --read-only  --company ID  --stats  --columns CSV  --print-payload
  --company runs ONE command as another company (ephemeral, not persisted) · ib help multi-tenancy

OUTPUT (JSON, stdout)
  { ok: true, ... } (raw backend response); --dry-run returns { dryRun: true, wouldUpdate: { <provided fields>, omittedFieldsPreserved: true } }

ERRORS (stderr, exit non-zero)
  exit 4 (client-side)  No fields to update    → pass at least one typed flag or a --body/--from-json patch
  exit 4 (HTTP 400)  Validation failed      → fix the patch fields
  exit 5 (HTTP 404)  Worksite not found     → verify tyomaaId
  exit 2 (HTTP 401)  Token expired          → ib auth refresh
  exit 3 (HTTP 403)  Permission denied      → check auth.page.tyomaa.edit
  exit 6 (HTTP 500)  Backend error          → retry with --verbose

NOTES
  - Prefer typed flags for the common fields — --comment maps to tyomaaMemo, --address to tyomaaOsoite1. Use --body/--from-json only for columns without a typed flag (e.g. rakennusDataJSON, asiakasId).
  - Address changes re-geocode the worksite server-side (lat/lng refresh).
  - Partial-update safety is server-side (tyomaa.setData read-merge, fb#234) — against an older backend without it, a partial body NULLs omitted columns. Verify with --dry-run first.

EXAMPLES
  ib worksite update 99 --comment "Pickup at gate B" --reason "gate info"
  ib worksite update 99 --address "Uusikatu 2" --postal-code 00100 --city Helsinki --reason "address fix"
  ib worksite update 99 --comment "" --reason "clear memo"
  ib worksite update 99 --body '{"tyomaaMemo":"Pickup at gate B"}' --reason "gate info"
"
`;
